From 95c713b1f9421efe4d16f325cce9ea30176b6938 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Leandro <academy@mindsofthefuture.com.br>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:27:51 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] health: Make the power_supply uevent BPF filter optional

On legacy 4.19 kernels the vendor bpfloader cannot load it, and a mandatory
program there aborts the boot (exit 121). HealthLoop already falls back to an
unfiltered uevent socket when the program is missing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I483140cac14168c044d69f9f6ee83b461d124a2b
---
 health/utils/libhealthloop/filterPowerSupplyEvents.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/health/utils/libhealthloop/filterPowerSupplyEvents.c b/health/utils/libhealthloop/filterPowerSupplyEvents.c
index 6f295c7..8495d42 100644
--- a/health/utils/libhealthloop/filterPowerSupplyEvents.c
+++ b/health/utils/libhealthloop/filterPowerSupplyEvents.c
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@ static long (*bpf_skb_load_bytes)(const struct __sk_buff* skb, int off, void* to
 #define HEX_POWER_SU 0x75735f7265776f70uLL  // "power_su"
 #define HEX_PPLY0    0x00000000796c7070uLL  // "pply\0" + null padding
 
-DEFINE_BPF_PROG("skfilter/power_supply", AID_ROOT, AID_SYSTEM, skfilter_power_supply)
+DEFINE_OPTIONAL_BPF_PROG("skfilter/power_supply", AID_ROOT, AID_SYSTEM, skfilter_power_supply)
 (struct __sk_buff* skb) {
     // The first character matched is a '\0'. Starting right past the netlink message header
     // is fine since the SUBSYSTEM= text never occurs at the start, as the kernel always
-- 
2.53.0

